format session-log-v1
stamp 20260819.133033
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan roster -- the supervisor derived from the declaration it obeys
prompt Autonomous loop: read the voice and the live cards, pick up the running thread, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds, send the finished increment.
think Read context/KYRI.md and context/RADIANT_STYLE.md first, so the voice shaped the lap from the first token, then crux/REMEMBER.md and the top rows of session-logs/README.md.
think Standfast checked before new work -- the living REDS rows (80 through 87) all read Closed or Released, so the line was clear and constructive work could open.
think The newest log's recommend named the crux exactly: teach a Caravan supervisor to take its child roster FROM a system document, so the declaration a witness checks is the same declaration the supervisor obeys. Lindy-first crux-first agreed -- the Microkernel Target double-seat leads, and this is the decisive move that makes every prior ring load-bearing rather than descriptive.
think Read the ground before writing: capabilities.rye (CapabilityTable, ChildSlot, right bits, Refusal), regions.rye (Map, Perm, Grant, refusal_reason), system.rye (System gathering graph and map, verify, Verdict), read.rye (bounded load from disk, LoadError). The five rings each declared one thing well and left one gap between them.
think Named the gap plainly -- the declaration described a system while the supervisor held its roster somewhere else. Two sources of truth wearing one architecture's name is the oldest way a proof stops meaning anything, so the roster is DERIVED rather than written beside.
think Found the load-bearing bound while reading: capabilities.max_children is 4 and regions.max_domains is 8, so a legal declaration can outrun the table. Chose to refuse by name (TooManyDomains) rather than seat what fits -- the same honesty read.rye spends a byte of headroom on, and the refusal names the SUPERVISOR's bound rather than a fault in the document.
think Chose two checkable properties over tidiness: conservation (every declared grant seats exactly one capability, so the counts must match) and agreement (the whole region-by-domain cross product at read, write, and execute each, table answer equal to map answer). The walk is total rather than sampled, which is what makes agreement a fact.
think Wrote caravan/systems/wide_roster.bron so the distinction is visible on disk -- five wired domains around one shared region, whole by every property verify reads, and still past four children.
think Built and ran: GREEN on the first metal pass. Refused to trust that -- proved the RED path by widening rights_of with one right the document withheld, rebuilt, and watched the agreement assert abort at check_serial_stack (exit 134). Restored the source and removed the probe binary.
obs W xor X crosses the translation for free. A grammar holding r, rw, rx and nothing else cannot derive a mask carrying write beside execute, so the property is inherited by construction rather than re-checked -- structure doing the work a later check would otherwise repeat.
obs The negative answers carry the round. A client reaching a buffer it was never granted is the failure this whole arc exists to rule out, and both rings refuse it, each in its own vocabulary: the map answers not_granted, the table answers no_such_resource. Two independent paths agreeing on a no is stronger evidence than either path agreeing on a yes.
obs Council rota lap item 21 -- ORGANIZING.md. Its placement law confirmed this round's filing without a second thought: implementation goes to the module it belongs to, the witness to tools/, the artifact beside its readers under caravan/systems/. Its "references are promises" line governed the docs-sync touch in the same commit.
obs Kept the round narrow -- one keystone, one new module, one new artifact, one witness, the README section that describes it, and the live card repointed. No unrelated sweep opened.
loom witness=caravan_roster_witness result=GREEN domains=3 grants=6 capabilities=6 wide_domains=5 red_probe_exit=134
file caravan/roster.rye the supervisor's capability table derived from the parsed declaration -- conservation and agreement both checkable, the roster bound refused by name
file caravan/systems/wide_roster.bron a whole declaration that still outruns this supervisor, so the bound belongs visibly to the table rather than to the document
file tools/caravan_roster_witness.rish proves the derivation on metal -- conservation, the shared refusal, the roster bound, and the grammar still refusing rwx before a roster is ever derived
file caravan/README.md the ladder row and the "Why the Supervisor Reads the Same Sentences" section, seated after the reader section in ring order (docs-sync in the same commit)
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge repointed single-stranded to six green rings and the next crux, the prior edge's per-ring prose already condensed
recommend keep-going -- the document and the supervisor now read the same sentences, so the next crux is the last step outward: a supervision loop that spawns its children FROM a roster and refuses a spawn the declaration never granted, closing the path from document to running process. No key, no funds.
